[h1]New World: Paradox Tinto[/h1]

The New World is the Paradox Tinto logo: a great landmass with its rays of islands and the lettering below, drawn with the generator's Land from an image feature. The Old World remains unchanged.

[h2]🌎 World[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Natives:[/b] 149 states and 166 tribes on 2,425 locations.
[*][b]Powers:[/b] One great empire of 30 locations, two regional powers, a maritime league and seven holy sites.
[*][b]Islands:[/b] All 49 vanilla island groups stay in the open sea, and 18 of them are moved to new waters.
[*][b]Resources:[/b] Gold, silver, gems and pearls at twice their vanilla frequency, and five exceptional places: a great silver lode, a rich silver vein, a silver seam, a mercury lode and a rich fishery.
[*][b]Settings:[/b] Native population at 180% of the vanilla New World, extraordinary peoples more likely, a turbulent past and slightly larger locations.
[/list]

[h2]▶ How to play[/h2]
Subscribe, enable this map in your playset and start a new 1337 campaign. You do not need the RNW generator to play it. Use one RNW world at a time, restart EU5 when switching maps, and keep this world mod for its saves.

Generated with RNW 1.2.1 on EU5 1.4.7, so continue its campaigns on that exact game version. Across the Pillars is optional.

[h2]🔗 Generator[/h2]
Made with [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3829217331]Random New World[/url]. The land comes from an image, so there is no World Code: a code cannot remake this map. To draw your own shape, paint land white and sea black and load it with [b]Land from an image[/b] in the generator.

